 **Evaluate:** Every requirement from `00 Frame.md` and every WAF pillar must be addressed. The recommendation must be falsifiable: it states which assumption, if wrong, would change the recommendation. Open questions are resolved with the developer before Solution begins. A closing WAF assessment runs on the recommended option only. `02 Evaluate.md` is written to disk for IDE review before the WAF assessment runs. Loops per decision under the same multi-decision policy as Research.
 
-**Solution:** Certainty principle applies. `Architecture.md` is the authoritative integrated end-to-end solution record: it carries every settled decision from Frame, Research, Evaluate, developer clarification, WAF and review feedback, with affected flows, consequences and verification obligations. `solution/` files contain only settled decisions and their direct consequences — no rationale, rejected alternatives or open questions. `Design.md`, `Stack.md` and `Efforts.md` provide supporting detail and must not introduce a material decision absent from or conflicting with Architecture.md. Each file is written to disk for IDE review as it is completed. After `Architecture.md` is confirmed, an optional `{{DESIGN_ARCHITECT_AGENT}}` read-only review gate checks structural completeness before `Design.md` is started (see `patterns/design-architect-review.md`). A WAF review gate (`patterns/waf-review.md`, target `solution`) runs after all four files are confirmed. `Efforts.md` must include an Operational Costs section (ongoing infra consumption at expected scale). Under the multi-decision policy, `Design.md` loops per decision but `Architecture.md` stays a single integrated file — one section per decision. Publish and `/dev` consume Architecture.md as the solution source of truth.
